steps:
1. In crates/downloader/Cargo.toml — add dependencies:
   suppaftp = { version = "6.3.0", default-features = false, features = ["async-rustls"] }
   NOTE: suppaftp 6.x 'async-rustls' enables FTPS over rustls; the sync path (no 'async' feature) gives the plain FTP client we'll use with spawn_blocking. Actually for 6.x we want the SYNC API — do NOT enable 'async' feature. Enable only features needed for FTPS TLS:
   suppaftp = { version = "6.3.0", default-features = false, features = ["rustls"] }
   This gives NativeTlsStream-equivalent via rustls for FTPS; plain FTP uses the non-TLS path.

4. In crates/downloader/src/lib.rs — add:
   mod ftp;
   pub use ftp::{FtpEngine, FtpEngineConfig};

6. In crates/core-services/src/config.rs — add:
   pub struct FtpConfig { pub enabled: bool, pub passive_mode: bool }
   impl Default for FtpConfig { enabled: true, passive_mode: true }
   Add ftp: FtpConfig field to EngineConfig with #[serde(default)].
   No new validation needed (enabled is a bool, passive_mode is a bool).

11. In crates/android-bridge/src/service.rs — update add_download to detect ftp/ftps schemes:
   Before the existing call to add_download_for_engine with DirectHttp, parse the scheme:
   if url.starts_with("ftp://") { engine = EngineKind::Ftp }
   else if url.starts_with("ftps://") { engine = EngineKind::Ftps }
   else { engine = EngineKind::DirectHttp }
   FTP/FTPS on Android work without changes since they are pure Rust.
